design test components enables the creation of high-performance components with a very small initial investment
when compared to traditional manufacturing techniques.
Considering the above, advantages of particular value to work undertaken in this study include the utilization of
cost-effective production, rapid prototyping and improving performance through lightweighting and geometric
complexity. The primary research objectives of this study are therefore as follows:
• To performe extensive research into the advantages and practical use-cases for AM in aerospace
components
• To investigate material characteristics and manufacturing processes of various AM engineering alloys
• To design, manufacture and test iterations of pump components in order to assess the practicality of using
AM for liquid rocket engine component fabrication
• To investigate and optimize the production of an injector flange component within the framework of AM
process characteristics
