chamber, nozzle, and cooling channels into one single component [417]. The nozzle is designed to be printed
using metal AM techniques allowing for a high complexity in design. The prototype, shown below in Figure 2-22,
is designed to be manufactured from Inconel 718 on an EOS M400-4 printer. The nozzle features a gyroid minimal
surface lattice design on its outer surface. These lattice structures are found in nature and are often self-supporting


41
and feature zero average curvature at any point on their surface, making for more even distribution of stresses
within the structures [318]. These examples demonstrate some of the potential, but these designs are still not
widely tested or adopted in flight components and currently are still in design and proof of concept phases.
