To calculate Sa values, for each deviation, the absolute value of the deviation is multiplied by the surface area,
and the sum is divided by the total surface area. In the same way that roughness is often calculated as the
arithmetical mean height of a line (Ra) values, linear measurements can be found by downscaling the data or by
using a line fit instead of a surface area calculation. With 3D data, roughness measurements can be performed for
both Ra and Sa values, but the Sa measurement is usually preferred, because it is less subject to variation.
