For the purposes of testing the defects present in low angle, unsupported surfaces on AM as-built components,
“overhang” samples were manufactured for all candidate materials (Ti-6Al-4V, 316L, MS1, 6061-T6) under
investigation for the SAFFIRE programme. The characteristics of unsupported surfaces built using AM for build
angles above 45 degrees are well known and therefore, the primary low angle range of interest was chosen as 25
– 55 degrees. This was achieved using samples (Figure 3-6) that contain various flat surfaces at angles stepped in
5-degree increments from 25 – 55 degrees from the build plane. Importantly, these samples contain a constant
wall thickness at each angle increment to ensure no wall thickness defects are present when comparing angles.
The scale of these samples was determined to ensure that the MicroCT scanning quality was high, and to find
relevant data for similar-scale geometric features present in SAFFIRE programme designs.


